[E0414] Error: cannot assign to `slot` while an `is` binding refers to it
    ╭─[ err/459_a_kept_borrow_of_a_binding_holds_its_place/main.wip:14:9 ]
    │
 12 │     if slot is .Some(value) {
    │        ──┬─
    │          ╰─── tested here; the bindings refer to it
    │
 14 │         slot = .None
    │         ──┬─
    │           ╰─── assigned here
    │
    │ Note: the bindings of an `is` test on a place are aliases for its fields, so the place must not change until the block ends
────╯
[E0436] Error: `marker.at` is used after `slot`, which it borrows, was changed
    ╭─[ err/459_a_kept_borrow_of_a_binding_holds_its_place/main.wip:15:16 ]
    │
 13 │         val marker = Marker(at: &value)
    │             ───┬──
    │                ╰──── `marker` borrows `slot`
 14 │         slot = .None
    │         ──┬─
    │           ╰─── `slot` assigned here
 15 │         assert(marker.at == 7)
    │                ────┬────
    │                    ╰────── used here
    │
    │ Help: use `marker.at` before `slot` changes, or keep a value that owns its data
    │
    │ Note: a view points into what it borrows — a `str` into bytes, a `&` into a place — so that must not change while the view is still used
────╯
